---
import RedlineLayout from '../layouts/RedlineLayout.astro';
import RedlineCTA from '../components/redline/RedlineCTA.astro';
---

<RedlineLayout
  title="About · Herru Adi"
  description="I'm Herru Adi, a strategic design partner with 9+ years working across fintech, AI, SaaS, and enterprise products. I bring the kind of thinking that shapes what gets built, not just how it looks."
  active="about"
>
  <style>
    .about-body {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 260px 1fr;
      gap: 48px;
      padding: 56px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    @media (max-width: 860px) {
      .about-body {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 24px;
      }
    }
    .about-photo {
      border: 1.5px solid var(--line-strong);
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-end;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
      background: var(--paper-deep);
    }
    .about-photo img {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover;
    }
    .about-photo .card {
      position: relative;
      margin: 14px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
      background: var(--paper);
      padding: 10px 12px;
      width: calc(100% - 28px);
    }
    .about-photo .card .name {
      font-family: var(--display);
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    .about-photo .card .role {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 10.5px;
      color: var(--ink-faint);
      margin-top: 2px;
    }
    .about-prose {
      font-family: var(--body);
      font-size: 16.5px;
      line-height: 1.85;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      max-width: 66ch;
    }
    .about-prose p {
      margin-bottom: 22px;
    }
    .about-prose p.emphasis {
      color: var(--ink);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .about-prose .principle {
      color: var(--ink);
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .about-section-label {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      color: var(--ink-faint);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: 22px;
    }
    .human-fields {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      gap: 20px 32px;
      margin-top: 8px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .human-fields {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }
    .human-fields dt {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      color: var(--ink-faint);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }
    .human-fields dd {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 15px;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
  </style>

  <!-- ============ PAGE HERO ============ -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Personnel File</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">I'm not here to execute your brief.</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">I ask the uncomfortable questions first. Then I design.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ WHO I AM ============ -->
  <section class="about-body">
    <div class="about-photo">
      <img src="/images/about.jpg" alt="Herru Adi" width="1200" height="1500" />
      <div class="card">
        <p class="name">Herru Adi</p>
        <p class="role">Strategic Design Partner</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="about-section-label">Who I Am</p>
      <div class="about-prose">
        <p>
          I started as a frontend developer, close enough to design to fall in love with it, far
          enough to understand how things get built.
        </p>
        <p>The switch wasn't planned. But once I crossed over, I never looked back.</p>
        <p>
          Nine years later, what keeps me here isn't the craft, it's the impact. A product I
          designed helping a kitchen run smoother. An app that actually solves someone's real
          problem. An agency that lands a client because the work looked and felt right. Small
          ripples, maybe. But ripples matter.
        </p>
        <p>
          I live by one principle: <span class="principle">hidup harus berguna bagi sesama</span>.
          Life should be useful to others. It's why I design, why I'm honest with clients even
          when it's uncomfortable, and why I named my son Gunaka Sasama, Sundanese for useful to
          others.
        </p>
        <p class="emphasis">That's not a tagline. That's just who I am.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ HOW I WORK ============ -->
  <section class="about-body" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr;">
    <div>
      <p class="about-section-label">How I Work</p>
      <div class="about-prose">
        <p class="emphasis">My process starts with one question: is this actually the problem?</p>
        <p>
          Before I open Figma, I want to understand what we're really solving. I break down the
          problem, challenge the assumptions, and make sure we're building the right thing, not
          just building things right. If something doesn't make sense, we talk it through.
          Designing the wrong solution is just expensive guesswork.
        </p>
        <p class="emphasis">That said, I know when to drive and when to fall in.</p>
        <p>
          When there's a PM or PO with a solid PRD on the table, I'm heads down and executing with
          precision. I respect process, I respect structure, and I know how to work within a
          system without losing the quality of the output.
        </p>
        <p class="emphasis">Two modes. One standard: make it count.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ THE HUMAN SIDE ============ -->
  <section class="about-body" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr; border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--line-strong);">
    <div>
      <p class="about-section-label">The Human Side</p>
      <dl class="human-fields">
        <div>
          <dt>Family</dt>
          <dd>A dad who does the school run every morning for my 4-year-old. Honestly, the best part of my day.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Off the clock</dt>
          <dd>Two wheels, Bandung's streets, roads I've never taken before. I keep telling myself I'll pick up music again soon.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>The bigger dream</dt>
          <dd>A design studio, and a free learning space for people who want to build in tech but can't afford the privilege of education. Not someday. Just not today yet.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Status</dt>
          <dd>Reviewing new engagements for Q4 2026.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <RedlineCTA />
</RedlineLayout>
